Z||000000||hugh||11-23-2000||07:49 AM|||| This thread is prompted by FieroLisa's problem.It may have been done before, but even if it has,let's update it.How about listing any places you feel are honest and do good work,specially if they know Fieros,but not limited to Fieros.There is a small tire and alignment shop near me that I trust.Blaese's in Berlin,NJ.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||11-23-2000||11:53 AM||||I have a few shops that I use:<BR>Paint and body work: Ty's Restored Rides, Oxford Alabama.<BR>Suspension alignments: Grover and Son's, Oxford AL.<BR>Muffler/Exhaust: Steve Crow at Faulkner Brother's, Choccolocco AL.<BR>These are the best in my area and usually don't mind Fiero projects!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Patrick's Dad||11-23-2000||11:58 AM||||I've only trusted one person with the repairs to my baby that I couldn't do because of time, tools, or safety, such as brakes and steering (I used to drive Patrick in her. If I broke her engine, then she couldn't go anywhere and she couldn't hurt anyone.):<P>Mark Millis of Sunset Auto in Braintree MA. He hates them, but not enough to turn down the (fair) $$.<P>------------------<BR>This should work until my site comes online....   <IMG SRC="http://homestead.deja.com/user.rshuman/files/Tmh.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroLisa||11-23-2000||05:00 PM||||Well Portage Motors in Brimfield, OH always did a fine job with the Fiero..charged a BIT more than I thought necessary, but then again always got it done right the first time, and on time. Too bad I just don't live there anymore.<BR>I have a good painter too, Glenn Butram from Cleveland OH...<BR>That's about it. AAMCO and AATCO are both worthless, the ones I've been to. I went to a GM dealer in Kent OH who did my throttle cable, but it cost me over $200 to do it...although it was fixed.<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/||||reg||1
Z||000004||Philphine||11-23-2000||06:46 PM||||hunt and knight. they only work on gm cars (i've been there to see them turn other makes away and/or recommend another shop) and specialise in corvettes. taken my '87 there twice for pretty major repairs (for me anyway). costly, but how often do you find cheap auto repair. friendly and explain the work they do.<P>i first went there with a vette i wanted to buy. they checked it over, gave me a list of what they found in the order of what should be repaired first to last with prices. they've fixed things they noticed free if it were really minor. once they did a fairly costly repair free and another were it broke while they had it so they put a part they had around the shop on it (power steering pump) gave me a big discount since it was used and work i didn't authorise.<P>i stil hate taking any car to a shop but there i don't feel like i'm gonna be jipped if they get a chance to do it.  <p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 11-23-2000).]||||reg||1
